/S /H3
/P 175 0 R
/T (Why Full Retrain Every Time?)
/E (Why Full Retrain Every Time?)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 175 0 R
/T (Preventing "Catastrophic Forgetting")
/E (Preventing "Catastrophic Forgetting")
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (If you only train a model on the newest 20 logs, the model physically overwrites its internal weights to fit those 20 logs. It will completely forget the behavioral patterns it learned from the first 100 logs.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 702 0 R
/E (Example: A user buys a laptop in month 1, and buys a mouse in month 2. If you only train incrementally on month 2, the model forgets the user owns that specific laptop. A full retrain ensures the model sees the entire journey and context.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 175 0 R
/T (The Data Scale Permits It)
/E (The Data Scale Permits It)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (In massive systems like Amazon \(billions of logs\), full retraining is too computationally expensive, so they are forced to use complex incremental learning streams. However, in our system, the data size per user is small \(a few hundred to a few thousand logs max\). Training a CatBoost model on 1,000 rows takes less than 2 seconds. Therefore, full retraining is perfectly viable and guarantees the highest possible accuracy)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 175 0 R
/T (Simplicity and Stability)
/E (Simplicity and Stability)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 175 0 R
/T (Incremental learning \(online learning\) requires highly complex architecture to manage learning rates decay, concept drift, and catastrophic forgetting mitigation. Batch learning \(full retrain\) is mathematically stable, highly reproducible, and much easier to debug for a proof-of-concept project.)
/E (Incremental learning \(online learning\) requires highly complex architecture to manage learning rates decay, concept drift, and catastrophic forgetting mitigation. Batch learning \(full retrain\) is mathematically stable, highly reproducible, and much easier to debug for a proof-of-concept project.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
