338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 180 0 R
/T (Methodology)
/E (Methodology)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (NCF is "Collaborative": NCF learns from the entire community. If NCF notices that User A and User B both buy similar laptops, and User A suddenly buys a camera, NCF learns that User B might also want that camera.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (Why Neural over Traditional Matrix Factorization? Traditional methods just multiply the User Vector by the Item Vector. That is a linear operation.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E ( E-commerce behavior is highly non-linear. The deep layers \(MLP\) in NCF can learn complex, hidden interactions that simple math misses.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (Complications & Simplifications:-)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (1.The Extreme Sparsity Problem:- We have 1.4 million products . A highly active user might view 100 products that means 99.99% of the user item matrix is completely empty .Neural networks struggle to learn when almost all data is missing .)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (We do not train NCF every time a user clicks something. NCF is trained globally offline as a heavy background job.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (2.The Cold Start Problem:- If a brand new user registers today, they have no ID embedding in the trained network. The NCF model literally cannot make a prediction for them until it is fully retrained.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (Fallback Mechanisms \(Handling Cold Start\): If NCF encounters a completely new user, the system gracefully falls back to showing "Global Trending/Best Sellers" until the next global retraining cycle happens.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (3.Computational Expense: Unlike CatBoost, which trains on one user's data in 2 seconds, training a global neural network on millions of logs across all users takes massive computational power \(GPUs\) and time \(minutes to hours\). It cannot be done in real-time.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (Memory-Efficient Embeddings: Instead of one-hot encoding 1.4 million products \(which would crash the RAM\), we use PyTorchnn.Embedding layers to map sparse IDs directly into dense 32-dimensional vectors, keeping memory usage drastically low.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
