374 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 184 0 R
/T (If standard SQL database search \(shoes\) works, why go through the trouble of building a complex semantic search?)
/E (If standard SQL database search \(shoes\) works, why go through the trouble of building a complex semantic search?)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
375 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 184 0 R
/T (The Problem with Standard Search \(Keyword Matching\): If a user searches for "running shoes for flat feet", standard SQL looks for those exact words. If a product is titled "Orthopedic Athletic Footwear", standard search will return zero results, even though it is exactly what the user wants. Keywords match letters, not intent.)
/E (The Problem with Standard Search \(Keyword Matching\): If a user searches for "running shoes for flat feet", standard SQL looks for those exact words. If a product is titled "Orthopedic Athletic Footwear", standard search will return zero results, even though it is exactly what the user wants. Keywords match letters, not intent.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
376 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 184 0 R
/T (Why Semantic Search? Semantic search maps concepts into a 3D-like space \(actually 3-dimensional space\).)
/E (Why Semantic Search? Semantic search maps concepts into a 3D-like space \(actually 3-dimensional space\).)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
377 0 obj
